you: That's stealing.
justin[smile]: It's a good day. He'll be able to tell.
@bg dawn_street t=slow
@cam wide
@hide all
> Outside, the laundromat sign is on and the sky has gone the colour of the inside of a shell.
> Behind you, Studio 25 has no lights at all, and one door on the second floor propped open with a sneaker.
> You have walked away from a great many buildings. You know the feeling by heart: the lightness, the door already closing.
> This isn't that. There's a plastic 25 in your pocket and a Saturday in your week, and someone beside you walking slowly, on purpose, so that you arrive at the same time.
> Half a street ahead, seven people are arguing about breakfast. One of them has just noticed his bag is lighter.
> Justin counts you both in, under his breath. Not in eights. Just *one, two* — and then he stops counting, because you're already in step.
@ending justin_beside
@credits
@end

